{
  "title": "ISic001655. Epitaph of Nassiana",
  "body": "<div id=\"editions\"><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa, Jonathan Prag; edition source: <a href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/UC29MPZC\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/UC29MPZC</a></div><div id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  <div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <a id=\"al1-interpretive\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span>(Χρίστο)ς <br id=\"al2-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span>Χρισιάνης <br id=\"al3-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>σεμνῆς ἀγανό-<br id=\"al4-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span>φρονος̣ [ἠδ]ὲ φιλάν-<br id=\"al5-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span>δρ<span class=\"petraeligature\" title=\"Ligature: these characters are joined\">ο͡υ</span>  <span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νασσιανῆς\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νασσιανῆς\"><span class=\"petraeligature\" title=\"Ligature: these characters are joined\">Ν</span>ασσ̣ιανῆς</span></span> τύμ-<br id=\"al6-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span>βον εἰσορᾶς φίλε κίμενον <br id=\"al7-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">7</span>[ὥδε ἥ]τ̣ις σεμνοσύνησιν <br id=\"al8-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">8</span>[ἐρίζε]το <span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Πηνελοπίη\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Πηνελοπίη\">Πηνελοπίη</span></span> ⸙ <br id=\"al9-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">9</span>☧ <br id=\"al10-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">10</span>[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] ἐνθάδε κῖτε <br id=\"al11-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">11</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νασσιανὴ\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νασσιανὴ\">[Νασσ]ιανὴ</span></span> ζήσασα <br id=\"al12-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">12</span>[ἐν? Θεῷ?] καλῶ<span class=\"small\" title=\"small character: ς\">ς</span> καὶ ἀμέμ-<br id=\"al13-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">13</span><span dir=\"ltr\">(vac.1)</span>πτως ἔτη <span class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">λβ</span>´ <br id=\"al14-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">14</span>μῆνας ·ι´· </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\">l.2 reg., orig. Χρισιάνης</p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa, Jonathan Prag; edition source: <a href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/UC29MPZC\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/UC29MPZC</a></div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span>☧Σ<br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span>ΧΡΙΣΙΑΝΗΣ<br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>ΣΕΜΝΗΣΑΓΑΝΟ<br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span>ΦΡΟΝΟ.[..]ΕΦΙΛΑΝ<br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span>ΔΡ<span class=\"petraeligature\" title=\"Ligature: these characters are joined\">Ο͡Υ</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νασσιανῆς\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νασσιανῆς\"><span class=\"petraeligature\" title=\"Ligature: these characters are joined\">Ν</span>ΑΣ.ΙΑΝΗΣ</span></span>ΤΥΜ<br id=\"al6-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span>ΒΟΝΕΙΣΟΡΑΣΦΙΛΕΚΙΜΕΝΟΝ<br id=\"al7-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">7</span>[....].ΙΣΣΕΜΝΟΣΥΝΗΣΙΝ<br id=\"al8-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">8</span>[.....]ΤΟ<span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Πηνελοπίη\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Πηνελοπίη\">ΠΗΝΕΛΟΠΙΗ</span></span>⸙<br id=\"al9-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">9</span>☧<br id=\"al10-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">10</span>[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]ΕΝΘΑΔΕΚΙΤΕ<br id=\"al11-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">11</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νασσιανὴ\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νασσιανὴ\">[....]ΙΑΝΗ</span></span>ΖΗΣΑΣΑ<br id=\"al12-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">12</span>[......]ΚΑΛΩ<span class=\"small\" title=\"small character: ς\">Σ</span>ΚΑΙΑΜΕΜ<br id=\"al13-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">13</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;ΠΤΩΣΕΤΗ<span class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">ΛΒ</span><br id=\"al14-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">14</span>ΜΗΝΑΣ·Ι·</span></div><p class=\"miniapp\">l.2 reg., orig. Χρισιάνης</p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2><a href=\"ISic001655_tiled.tif\"><img title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo Museo Archeologico Regionale Paolo Orsi\" src=\"ISic001655_tiled-thumb.tif\"></a><a href=\"ISic001655.jpg\"><img title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo Museo Archeologico Regionale Paolo Orsi\" src=\"ISic001655-thumb.jpg\"></a></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span>  <span>Text of Ferrua 1940, controlled against photograph</span>  </span>; </li><li><span class=\"11\">11: <span>Ferrua suggests that a monogram of some sort may be missing before the name</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag</a></p>  <p>Friend, you see here laid out the tomb of Nassiane, a revered Christian, gentle of mood, loving of her husband, who competed with Penelope in virtue. Here lies Nassiane, having lived (in God?) well and blamelessly for 32 years, 10 months.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>The text was essentially established by Ferrua, who disposed of the speculative restorations of Strazzulla and clarified the various orthographic variations.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Orsi NSA 1895 509 no. 234 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001711\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001711</a></li><li> Orsi 1896 14 no. 13 (282) <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001710\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001710</a></li><li> Strazzulla 1897 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001565\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001565</a></li><li> Ferrua 1940 69 no.12 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002002\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002002</a></li><li> Agnello 1953 no.102 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002211\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002211</a></li><li> Rizzone 2011 262-263 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001631\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001631</a></li><li> Lamagna and Amato 2014 24 no.4 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001892\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001892</a></li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"><p>Lunate sigma and epsilon, cursive mu, uncial omega.</p> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.  </div>",
